[{:seon.cluster.eval/id "3112dd460857", :seon.cluster.eval/ordinal 0, :seon.cluster.eval/source "(help)", :seon.cluster.eval/comment ";; I should understand how this REPL works before I act.", :seon.eval/shown "The prompt shows your namespace my.agents.issue-family-proof and is drawn for you. Send only ;; thinking comments and forms.\nResults are data: chain them with ->>, sort-by, filter, map, and get-in. Functions are callable by their fully qualified symbols.\nForms are evaluated in order, and their results arrive in your NEXT turn. Act on a result only after you have seen it; do not complete a step in the same reply as the form that does the work.\nThe REPL supplies responses: :value (or :error) is result data, :out is printed text, and :result names the live value. Do not write responses yourself.\nresult/e... is a real symbol bound to the live value: evaluate it, pass it as an argument, or dig in with get-in and keys.\nWhen unsure, use (dir ns) first, for example (dir my.note). Copy the exact function name, including ! on mutations. (doc my.note/add!) gives its request keys, return shape and example. (dir my.agents.issue-family-proof) lists your own public functions and schema declarations.\nYour plan is your instructions. Read its current step and completion criterion before acting; a done-query completes it automatically when the facts match, and you mark a step without one complete only after seeing the result. Update an existing component by its identity or :db/id: a new identity-less nested map replaces it.\nRead incoming messages with a reverse-ref pull on your agent. (my.message/send {:my.message/to \"root\" :my.message/content \"...\"}) sends; sending does not end your turn. Remove an entity and its incoming refs with (seon.db/transact! [[:db.fn/retractEntity lookup-ref]]); retract removes only the named fact.\nUse pull for a known entity's shape, nested refs, and reverse refs such as :seon.message/_inbox; q for filters, joins, and aggregates; q with inner pull for filtering and shaping. (seon.db/transact! tx-data) writes. Your cluster database is supplied.\nDefine a function with its invoke contract: (defn increment {:malli/schema [:=> [:cat :int] :int]} [x] (+ x 1)). The input :cat describes the arguments; the last schema describes the result. A function that can fail returns [:or <success> :seon.error/value]; a bare :maybe is refused. [:vector X] needs a vector; use vec to convert a lazy seq. Admitted definitions are durable. Auto-check calls your function with generated inputs including each collection's empty value. A deftest becomes a durable test. deftest and is are referred; use clojure.test/testing with its namespace. (my.test/run) runs yours.\nA mistake returns :error data. Read the expected schema, offending value, and attribute candidates before retrying. Time is the transaction: a ref value \"datomic.tx\" names this write, for example (seon.db/transact! [{:my.note/id \"observation\" :my.note/agent [:seon.agent/id \"12254041a057\"] :my.note/content \"Verified\" :my.note/about \"datomic.tx\"}]); pull :db/txInstant through that ref.\nEach reply is one turn. (seon.turn/turns-left) reads your remaining turns; settings contain the configured limit. (my.agent/done) must be the last form of your reply; it ends your session early.\nTools: my.agent, my.background, my.edit, my.fs, my.issue, my.message, my.note, my.plan, my.shell, my.test, my.turn, my.web. Inspect one with dir.", :seon.eval/duration-ms 491} {:seon.cluster.eval/id "41ff802bc17e", :seon.cluster.eval/ordinal 1, :seon.cluster.eval/source "(seon.db/pull\n  '[:seon.agent/id {:seon.agent/namespace [:seon.ns/name {:seon.ns/steward [:seon.agent/id]}]}]\n  [:seon.agent/id \"12254041a057\"])", :seon.cluster.eval/comment ";; I should know my identity, namespace, and its steward.", :seon.eval/shown "#:seon.agent{:id \"12254041a057\", :namespace #:seon.ns{:name my.agents.issue-family-proof, :steward #:seon.agent{:id \"12254041a057\"}}}", :seon.eval/duration-ms 288} {:seon.cluster.eval/id "f9a3e0a36a42", :seon.cluster.eval/ordinal 2, :seon.cluster.eval/source "(seon.plan/plan {})", :seon.cluster.eval/comment ";; My plan is my instructions. No step is selected. my.plan/current! selects; completing clears the selection.", :seon.eval/shown "{:seon.agent/id \"12254041a057\"\n :my.plan/objective \"A run form's `:seon.fn/calls` edges are recorded for functions in the agent's\\nown namespace and for `my.*` toolkit functions, but NOT for a fully qualified\\ncore function the form plainly calls. `(seon.db/q '[...])` inside an agent form\\nproduces no edge to the `seon.db/q` entity, even though that entity exists in\\nthe same program graph.\\n\\nEvery \\\"which forms used this function?\\\" question is therefore silently wrong for\\ncore functions — the exact class the \\\"everything is queryable\\\" principle exists\\nto prevent. It is not a missing fact (the entity is there); it is a missing EDGE,\\nwhich is worse, because the query returns a confident empty answer.\"\n :seon.plan/step-lines {\"f073bb6553f5\" \"1. completed — Historical call-edge analyses need re-evaluation — 2026-09-16T02:33:46.746Z\"}\n :seon.plan/update-example \"(my.plan/current! {:my.plan.item/id \\\"f073bb6553f5\\\"})\"}", :seon.eval/duration-ms 345} {:seon.cluster.eval/id "8e04ecc86529", :seon.cluster.eval/ordinal 3, :seon.cluster.eval/source "(my.issue/status {:seon.issue/id \"agent-form-calls-to-core-namespaces-are-not-indexed\"})", :seon.cluster.eval/comment ";; My issue. Its tests define done; (my.test/check ...) runs them.", :seon.eval/shown "{:db/id 43695, :seon.issue/agent #:db{:id 55159}, :seon.issue/budget 1, :seon.issue/check-form (my.test/check #:seon.test{:changed [\"seon.test-reaching-test/agent-admitted-tests-reach-their-tested-function\"]}), :seon.issue/commits [\"5deb40e4e\" \"7e35df213\" \"924fdbf3a\" \"f402c5d3d\"], :seon.issue/functions #{\"Restart the JVM to remove stale loaded Var clojure.core/=; it is absent from the published program graph.\" \"Restart the JVM to remove stale loaded Var clojure.core/let; it is absent from the published program graph.\" \"Restart the JVM to remove stale loaded Var clojure.test/deftest; it is absent from the published program graph.\" \"Restart the JVM to remove stale loaded Var clojure.test/is; it is absent from the published program graph.\" \"Restart the JVM to remove stale loaded Var my.turn/wait; it is absent from the published program graph.\" \"Restart the JVM to remove stale loaded Var seon.db/db; it is absent from the published program graph.\" \"Restart the JVM to remove stale loaded Var seon.db/q; it is absent from the published program graph.\" \"Restart the JVM to remove stale loaded Var seon.fn/analyze-form; it is absent from the published program graph.\" \"Restart the JVM to remove stale loaded Var seon.fn/analyze-forms; it is absent from the published program graph.\" \"Restart the JVM to remove stale loaded Var seon.operator/connection; it is absent from the published program graph.\"}, :seon.issue/id \"agent-form-calls-to-core-namespaces-are-not-indexed\", :seon.issue/path \"docs/seon/issues/agent-form-calls-to-core-namespaces-are-not-indexed.md\", :seon.issue/problem \"A run form's `:seon.fn/calls` edges are recorded for functions in the agent's\\nown namespace and for `my.*` toolkit functions, but NOT for a fully qualified\\ncore function the form plainly calls. `(seon.db/q '[...])` inside an agent form\\nproduces no edge to the `seon.db/q` entity, even though that entity exists in\\nthe same program graph.\\n\\nEvery \\\"which forms used this function?\\\" question is therefore silently wrong for\\ncore functions — the exact class the \\\"everything is queryable\\\" principle exists\\nto prevent. It is not a missing fact (the entity is there); it is a missing EDGE,\\nwhich is worse, because the query returns a confident empty answer.\", :seon.issue/severity :friction, :seon.issue/status :open, :seon.issue/tests #{{:seon.issue.test/state :verified, :seon.test/error-count 0, :seon.test/fail-count 0, :seon.test/pass-count 7, :seon.test/run #:seon.test.run{:basis-t 536871460, :id \"710ed89b6b3a\"}, :seon.test/sym \"seon.test-reaching-test/agent-admitted-tests-reach-their-tested-function\"}}, :seon.issue/title \"Historical call-edge analyses need re-evaluation\"}", :seon.eval/duration-ms 331} {:seon.cluster.eval/id "5e64bcebc534", :seon.cluster.eval/ordinal 4, :seon.cluster.eval/source "(seon.db/pull\n  '[{:seon.message/_inbox\n     [:seon.message/id :seon.message/content {:seon.message/from [:seon.agent/id]}]}]\n  [:seon.agent/id \"12254041a057\"])", :seon.cluster.eval/comment ";; I should follow incoming messages with a reverse-ref pull on myself.", :seon.eval/shown "nil", :seon.eval/duration-ms 163} {:seon.cluster.eval/id "552293d632f0", :seon.cluster.eval/ordinal 5, :seon.cluster.eval/source "(seon.agent/settings)", :seon.cluster.eval/comment ";; My setting overrides; (seon.agent/effective-settings) shows inherited cluster defaults on demand.", :seon.eval/shown "{:seon.config.ai/no-provider true, :seon.config.run/max-episode-runs 1}", :seon.eval/duration-ms 385} {:seon.cluster.eval/id "5002df802582", :seon.cluster.eval/ordinal 6, :seon.cluster.eval/source "(get\n  (seon.db/pull\n    '[{:my.note/_agent [:my.note/id :my.note/content {:my.note/about [:my.plan.item/id]}]}]\n    [:seon.agent/id \"12254041a057\"])\n  :my.note/_agent\n  [])", :seon.cluster.eval/comment ";; I should read my saved notes; an empty read will observe the first note I add.", :seon.eval/shown "[]", :seon.eval/duration-ms 156} {:seon.cluster.eval/id "e1b8b8cf9964", :seon.cluster.eval/ordinal 7, :seon.cluster.eval/source "(dir my.agents.issue-family-proof)", :seon.cluster.eval/comment ";; I should inspect what I have defined and which schemas I declared.", :seon.eval/shown "{:seon.repl/columns [:sym :arglists :doc :in :out], :seon.repl/rows [], :seon.repl/schemas {}}", :seon.eval/duration-ms 333} {:seon.cluster.eval/id "2ea3ca00edab", :seon.cluster.eval/ordinal 8, :seon.cluster.eval/source "(seon.db/pull\n  '[{:seon.agent/runtime\n     [{:seon.runtime/trigger\n       [:seon.message/id :seon.message/content {:seon.message/from [:seon.agent/id]}]}\n      {:seon.runtime/listens [:seon.listen/attribute :seon.listen/entity :seon.listen/value]}]}]\n  [:seon.agent/id \"12254041a057\"])", :seon.cluster.eval/comment ";; My trigger and listens; (seon.db/pull '[{:seon.agent/runtime [:seon.runtime/turns]}] [:seon.agent/id \"12254041a057\"]) reads my turns on demand.", :seon.eval/shown "nil", :seon.eval/duration-ms 142} {:seon.cluster.eval/id "c38adaf5ad56", :seon.cluster.eval/ordinal 9, :seon.cluster.eval/source "(seon.db/q\n  '[:find\n    [(pull ?error [* {:seon.error/fn [:db/id :seon.fn/sym]} {:seon.error/occurrences [*]}]) ...]\n    :in\n    $\n    ?id\n    :where\n    [?agent :seon.agent/id ?id]\n    [?namespace :seon.ns/steward ?agent]\n    [?function :seon.fn/ns ?namespace]\n    [?error :seon.error/fn ?function]]\n  \"12254041a057\")", :seon.cluster.eval/comment "; Inspect errors in the namespaces assigned to me.", :seon.eval/shown "[]", :seon.eval/duration-ms 156}]